      "message": "I was looking at `KVM_CAP_X86_APIC_BUS_CYCLES_NS` in generic kvm and they have this validation:\n\n```\n»       »       /*\n»       »        * Guard against overflow in tmict_to_ns(). 128 is the highest\n»       »        * divide value that can be programmed in APIC_TDCR.\n»       »        */\n»       »       r \u003d -EINVAL;\n»       »       if (!bus_cycle_ns ||\n»       »           check_mul_overflow((u64)U32_MAX * 128, bus_cycle_ns, \u0026unused))\n»       »       »       break;\n```\n\nsince we are validating 0 to to be invalid, I think it would be worth to have this check in pKVM as well. WDYT?",
