      "side": 1,
      "message": "In pKVM we are only using this `kvm-\u003earch.apic_bus_cycle_ns` value for calculating the LAPIC clock frequency in `kvm_cpuid()`:\n\n```\n/*\n * Core crystal clock must match the LAPIC clock.\n * See native_calibrate_tsc().\n */\n*ecx \u003d 1000000000 / vcpu-\u003ekvm-\u003earch.apic_bus_cycle_ns;\n```\n\nand the only reason we are validating it here is to prevent division by zero.\n\nAPIC_TDCR and most other APIC registers are, by design, emulated by the host, not by pKVM. So there is no particular reason for pKVM to care about that and duplicate the overflow check already done by the host?\n\nBTW that solution for exposing TSC frequency I implemented in aosp/3956675 is not perfect, we might replace it with something else in the future, and then we might not use `apic_bus_cycle_ns` in pKVM at all (and if so, won\u0027t need to validate it at all).",
